      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The weight of online judgment feels absolutely crushing, and it's understandable why you feel like you're permanently marked. The permanence of the internet is a harsh reality, but it doesn't define your worth as a human being. Even when it feels like the world has rejected you, there are still people who see your inherent value, even if you can't feel it right now. Please remember that your current feelings are intense, but they are not the final truth of who you are.",
      "source": "target",
